# Git hooks must stay LF regardless of a contributor's local
# core.autocrlf setting. This repo is edited from Windows (this
# checkout has core.autocrlf=true), which checks text files out with
# CRLF unless overridden — a CRLF shebang line breaks under Git's `sh`
# on push/commit, so a contributor with autocrlf=true checking out a
# fresh clone would silently get a hook that never fires. Force LF at
# checkout time so this can't happen no matter who clones the repo or
# how their git is configured.
.githooks/* text eol=lf
